{{also|Westen}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|wēsten||a desert, waste}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*wōstinjō||a waste, wilderness}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*wāsto-||empty, wasted}}. Cognate with {{etyl|fy|-}} {{m|fy|woastyn||desert}}, {{etyl|stq|-}} {{m|stq|wustenej||desert}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|woestijn||desert}}, {{etyl|fr|-}} {{m|fr|gâtine||wasteland, moor}} (, from {{etyl|gem|-}}), {{etyl|gmh|-}} {{m|gmh|wuostinne||desert, wilderness}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|Wüste||desert}}). More at {{l|en|westy}}, {{l|en|waste}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|obsolete}} A [[waste]], [[wasteland]]; [[desert]].

----

